#!/bin/bash
# Serve Muse Glimmer 30B with the locally-built sm120 vLLM image.
#
#   ./run-muse                                   # RedHatAI/Muse-Glimmer-30B-NVFP4
#   ./run-muse meta-models/Muse-Glimmer-30B      # the original bf16 checkpoint
#   ./run-muse --selftest                        # offline check of the ATEM parsers
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY NVFP4 IS THE DEFAULT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Single-stream decode is memory-bandwidth bound: every weight is read once per
# token. The bf16 checkpoint is 52.9 GB of text-model weights, and this card
# sustains roughly 1.6-1.8 TB/s, so the ceiling is ~30-34 tok/s. Measured: 27.
# That is 80-90% of the roofline -- there is no software fix, the bytes are the
# bytes.
#
# RedHatAI/Muse-Glimmer-30B-NVFP4 quantizes the 416 block linears to FP4 (W4A4,
# compressed-tensors) and leaves lm_head, embed_tokens and the whole vision
# tower in bf16. Per-token read drops to roughly 14 GB, moving the roofline to
# ~120 tok/s. That is where the speed is; everything else in this file is worth
# single-digit percentages by comparison.
#
# It also explains the model card's numbers. Its "74.9 -> 233.4 tok/s (3.1x)"
# was measured on the K-Quant-17GB build, not bf16 -- the speculative speedup
# sits ON TOP of quantization, which is why DFlash alone never got close.
#
# The drafter borrows the target's embed_tokens and lm_head, and this recipe
# leaves both unquantized (`targets: ["Linear"]`, lm_head in `ignore`), so
# SPEC=1 still composes. It is off by default -- see the SPEED section.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THIS SCRIPT EXISTS (and why ./run produces loops/garbage on "Hi")
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# vLLM has NO native MuseGlimmerForConditionalGeneration implementation
# (checked on 0.25.2 and again on 0.27.1.dev0: ModelRegistry.get_supported_archs()
# has no Muse* arch, and no muse/glimmer/atem parser in either registry).
# transformers 5.15 DOES, so vLLM silently falls back to its generic Transformers
# backend (TransformersMultiModalForCausalLM), which logs only a mild "no vLLM
# implementation" warning and then computes the model WRONG in two ways -- and
# leaves the wire format unparsed, which is the third.
#
# BUG 1 -- the dropped embedding norm. THIS is what wrecks the output.
#   Muse Glimmer's input embedding is not a plain nn.Embedding; it carries a
#   weight-less RMSNorm applied to every looked-up row --
#   transformers/models/muse_glimmer/modeling_muse_glimmer.py:436
#       class MuseGlimmerTextNormedEmbedding(nn.Embedding):
#           def forward(self, input_ids):
#               return self.embed_norm(super().forward(input_ids))
#   The fallback unconditionally swaps the input embedding for a plain
#   VocabParallelEmbedding (vllm/.../transformers/base.py:170-189). It knows
#   about a scalar `embed_scale`, but nothing about an `embed_norm` MODULE, so
#   the norm is silently dropped and layer 0 gets unnormalized embeddings.
#   Measured against stock HF on the same 57-token prompt, hidden states diverge
#   immediately: cosine 0.456 at layer 0, ~0.31 by layer 51. Output is garbage
#   (a burst of <|eom|> and stray CJK) or degenerate repetition.
#   FIXED HERE by patches/muse-embed-norm/sitecustomize.py, mounted on
#   PYTHONPATH. With it, all 52 layers match HF at cosine >= 0.9992 (the
#   remainder is ordinary bf16 kernel drift) and generation matches HF's.
#
# BUG 2 -- the dropped output multiplier. Real, but subtler.
#   vllm/model_executor/models/transformers/causal.py:58
#       logit_scale = getattr(self.text_config, "logit_scale", 1.0)
#   Muse Glimmer has no `logit_scale`. It calls the field `output_multiplier`
#   and applies it, plus a Gemma-style tanh softcap, in
#   MuseGlimmerForConditionalGeneration.forward -- i.e. AFTER the LM head, which
#   the fallback never calls -- modeling_muse_glimmer.py:1255
#       logits = logits * output_multiplier          # 0.19611613513818404
#       logits = logits / final_logit_softcapping    # / 20.0
#       logits = torch.tanh(logits) * final_logit_softcapping
#   So stock vLLM emits logits 1/0.196 = 5.1x TOO LARGE and uncapped, and the
#   recommended temperature=1.0 behaves like temperature ~0.2. Measured: with
#   BUG 1 fixed but this left alone, two runs of the same prompt at temp 1.0
#   came back byte-identical -- sampling had collapsed to greedy, which is the
#   standard precondition for repetition loops on longer agentic runs.
#   FIXED HERE by handing vLLM the multiplier under the name its fallback reads,
#   via --hf-overrides (see LOGIT_SCALE below). Runs then vary as they should.
#
#   Residual vs native HF: the tanh softcap is still not applied. It is
#   monotonic so it never reorders tokens, and after the 0.196 multiply the
#   logits sit well inside the +/-20 cap, so it only slightly compresses the
#   tail. Sampling stays a hair sharper than reference.
#
# Both workarounds exist only because there is no native implementation. When
# vLLM ships one, drop --hf-overrides AND the sitecustomize patch together. To
# re-verify after any vLLM bump: PATCH=0 ./run-muse and prompt "Hi" -- if the
# reply is coherent, the fallback no longer drops embed_norm.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BUG 3 -- no ATEM parser, so no reasoning split and no tool calls.
#   Muse Glimmer does NOT use <think>. Its chat template is a Harmony-style
#   ATEM format: `<|start|>assistant to=self<|message|>...<|eom|>` for reasoning,
#   `<|start|>assistant to=user<|message|>...` for the answer, and
#   `<atem:function_calls><atem:invoke name=...>` for tools. vLLM ships no
#   parser for it (no muse/glimmer/atem in the --tool-call-parser choices, none
#   in vllm/reasoning/__init__.py) and does not read the tokenizer's
#   `response_template` either, so /v1/chat/completions handed back the whole
#   transcript as `content` -- chain of thought, routing tokens and all -- and
#   any request carrying tools was rejected outright:
#       "auto" tool choice requires --enable-auto-tool-choice and
#       --tool-call-parser to be set
#   FIXED HERE by patches/atem-parsers/atem_parsers.py, a --tool-parser-plugin
#   + --reasoning-parser-plugin registered under the name `atem`. Reasoning
#   lands in `reasoning`, the answer in `content`, `<atem:invoke>` blocks come
#   back as OpenAI tool_calls, streaming included. `./run-muse --selftest`
#   checks it against vLLM's real parser plumbing without a GPU or a server.
#   PARSERS=0 ./run-muse goes back to raw transcripts (and 400s on tools).
#   Pointing the qwen3 parsers at this model makes things worse, not better.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPEED -- the DFlash drafter (SPEC=1; OFF by default, see the measurements)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Muse Glimmer ships a DFlash block-diffusion drafter, NOT an MTP head, so
# ./run's --speculative-config '{"method":"mtp"}' is the wrong knob. DFlash
# predicts a whole 16-token block in one forward pass and the target verifies
# the block in parallel. Model card: 74.9 -> 233.4 tok/s (3.1x) on an RTX 5090.
#     meta-models/Muse-Glimmer-30B-assistant   4.8 GB bf16, 5 layers, block 16
#
# DEFAULT OFF. It is a large win on short prompts and a NET LOSS past ~2k tokens
# of context, which is where agentic work lives. Measured on bf16, temp 1.0:
#     ctx   304   accept .895  len 14.42     ctx  4427  accept .121  len 2.81
#     ctx  1620   accept .236  len  4.54     ctx 16577  accept .043  len 1.65
# At 16k that is 21.3 tok/s against a 26.9 baseline. The step between 1620 and
# 2187 is the drafter's own 2048-token sliding window; the decay past it is the
# drafter running out of usable signal. See ./scripts/muse-spec-probe and the
# commit messages for 6da9c19.
#
# vLLM 0.27.1 supports the METHOD but not this CHECKPOINT. Four gaps:
#
#   * No aux hidden states -- THE ONE THAT KILLS THE SERVER. DFlash feeds on the
#     target's hidden states at layers {1,13,25,37,49}. vLLM's Transformers
#     backend advertises the EAGLE3 interface for this, but on Muse Glimmer it
#     captures NOTHING: transformers 5.15 keys capture off a module-level
#     registry populated in PreTrainedModel.__init__, and MuseGlimmerModel's
#     entry is None, so vLLM's `if ... is None: self.model._can_record_outputs
#     = {}` writes an instance attribute nothing reads. Three more layers of
#     breakage stack on it. Symptom: the container dies during the profile run
#     on `assert isinstance(model_output, tuple)`.
#     FIXED HERE by shim 2 in patches/muse-embed-norm/sitecustomize.py.
#   * No registered architecture. EAGLEConfig rewrites the draft's
#     architectures MuseGlimmerAssistantModel -> DFlashMuseGlimmerAssistantModel
#     (vllm/transformers_utils/configs/eagle.py:63-72) and that name is not in
#     _SPECULATIVE_DECODING_MODELS. A DFlash* name never falls through to the
#     Transformers backend either, so resolution hard-fails.
#     FIXED HERE by patches/muse-dflash/muse_dflash.py, registered with
#     --model-class-overrides. The drafter's layers are Qwen3-shaped verbatim,
#     so it is a thin subclass of vLLM's own DFlashQwen3ForCausalLM plus a
#     rename of the two `encoder.*` tensors.
#   * Wrong config key layout. The drafter puts mask_token_id/target_layer_ids
#     at the top level where vLLM wants a dflash_config dict, and ships no
#     vocab_size at all (it has no embedding table). --hf-overrides cannot fix
#     this: dict overrides are deliberately target-only
#     (vllm/config/speculative.py:639-663).
#     FIXED HERE by shim 3 in patches/muse-embed-norm/sitecustomize.py, which
#     wraps SpeculativeConfig.hf_config_override -- the same seam vLLM uses
#     in-tree to reshape every MTP checkpoint.
#   * Sliding-window KV vs absolute slot writes. All 5 draft layers are
#     sliding_attention, and DFlash writes context K/V at absolute cache slots.
#     Left alone, everything past 2048 tokens lands in the shared null block --
#     silent garbage, no error. FIXED HERE in muse_dflash.py by clearing the
#     window on the Attention module, as laguna_dflash.py:117-121 does.
#
# The drafter ships no embed_tokens and no lm_head, so it borrows both from the
# target. That is what makes BUG 2 matter twice over: rejection sampling
# compares draft logits against target logits, so LOGIT_SCALE is passed through
# to the drafter too (MUSE_DRAFT_LOGIT_SCALE) and the two must agree.
#
# TWO NON-OBVIOUS CONVENTIONS, both settled by the reference implementation that
# ships in the image at transformers/models/muse_glimmer_assistant/ (read it
# before changing either -- they are counter-intuitive and were guessed wrong
# the first time):
#   * The drafter embeds WITHOUT the target's embedding RMSNorm. See
#     DRAFT_EMBED_NORM below and the comment at modeling_muse_glimmer.py:436.
#   * The drafter's attention is NON-causal: inside the 16-token block the mask
#     tokens attend bidirectionally, including to later mask tokens. See
#     DRAFT_CAUSAL below.
#
# Verify with ./scripts/muse-spec-check -- a ~3 min EAGER=1 wiring check first,
# then it boots both ways and asserts the greedy token ids are identical, which
# is the sharp test: DFlash rejection sampling is output-preserving, so any
# divergence means the wiring is wrong.
#
# Other things ./run gets wrong for this model, all deliberately dropped here:
#
#   * NO NVFP4 --linear-backend
#       This checkpoint is bf16 ("dtype": "bfloat16", ~59.5 GB over 2 shards),
#       not NVFP4-quantized. The NVFP4 GEMM knobs are meaningless here.
#   * NO --kv-cache-dtype fp8 by default
#       This is a 32Q/2KV GQA model. With only 2 KV heads there is very little
#       redundancy to absorb fp8 KV quantization error. Opt in with KV_FP8=1.
#   * NO VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN / 262144 context
#       max_position_embeddings is 131072 and rope_type is "default" (no scaling),
#       so 262144 is pure out-of-distribution extrapolation.
#
# A/B knobs without editing this file:
#   PATCH=0 ./run-muse                 # drop the embed_norm patch -> garbage (BUG 1)
#   LOGIT_SCALE=1.0 ./run-muse         # stock vLLM logits -> greedy collapse (BUG 2)
#   PARSERS=0 ./run-muse               # drop the ATEM parsers -> raw transcript (BUG 3)
#   SPEC=0 ./run-muse                  # no drafter, plain autoregressive decode
#   SPEC_TOKENS=7 ./run-muse           # shorter draft block (default 15, = block_size-1)
#   DRAFT_CAUSAL=1 ./run-muse          # causal drafter attention (default: non-causal)
#   DRAFT_EMBED_NORM=1 ./run-muse      # drafter reads NORMED embeddings (default: raw)
#   EAGER=1 ./run-muse                 # no torch.compile / CUDA graphs
#   SWA=0 ./run-muse                   # don't hoist layer_types (see below)
#   KV_FP8=1 ./run-muse                # fp8 KV cache (quality risk, 2 KV heads)
#   REASONING=xhigh ./run-muse         # low | medium | high | xhigh
#   VISION=0 ./run-muse                # drop the perception encoder (text only)
#   ATTN_BACKEND=FLASH_ATTN ./run-muse   # default is flashinfer
#   LINEAR_BACKEND= ./run-muse           # let vLLM pick the NVFP4 GEMM
#   MAX_NUM_SEQS=3 ./run-muse            # the old, bf16-era concurrency
#   MAX_MODEL_LEN=32768 ./run-muse
#   IMAGE_TAG=cu1312-sm120 ./run-muse
#   EXTRA_ARGS="--max-num-seqs 8" ./run-muse
#
# Benchmark a variant against the running server: ./bench <label>
set -euo pipefail

NAME=vllm-muse
IMAGE=${IMAGE:-iphands/vllm-blackwell}
IMAGE_TAG=${IMAGE_TAG:-latest}
CONTAINER="$IMAGE:$IMAGE_TAG"

SELFTEST=0
[[ "${1:-}" == "--selftest" ]] && { SELFTEST=1; shift; }

# models/vllm is mounted whole at /models, rather than the model's own parent,
# because the NVFP4 build lives under RedHatAI/ while the DFlash drafter lives
# under meta-models/ -- they are no longer siblings, and a per-model mount cannot
# see both. MODEL/DRAFT are therefore paths RELATIVE to this root.
MODEL_ROOT=${MODEL_ROOT:-$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/models/vllm" && pwd)}
_arg=${1:-RedHatAI/Muse-Glimmer-30B-NVFP4}
if [[ -d "$_arg" ]]; then
  # A full path, as ./scripts/muse-spec-* pass. Keep it relative to the root when
  # it lives under it; otherwise fall back to mounting its own parent.
  _abs=$(cd "$_arg" && pwd)
  case "$_abs/" in
    "$MODEL_ROOT"/*) MODEL=${_abs#"$MODEL_ROOT"/} ;;
    *) MODEL_ROOT=$(dirname "$_abs"); MODEL=$(basename "$_abs") ;;
  esac
else
  MODEL=$_arg
fi
[[ -d "$MODEL_ROOT/$MODEL" ]] || {
  echo "no model at $MODEL_ROOT/$MODEL"
  echo "pass a path, or set MODEL_ROOT=. Available:"
  find "$MODEL_ROOT" -maxdepth 2 -name config.json -printf '  %h\n' 2>/dev/null | sed "s|$MODEL_ROOT/||"
  exit 1; }
MODEL_FOLDER=$MODEL_ROOT                          # what gets bind-mounted at /models

PORT=${PORT:-8700}                               # 8702: coexists with ./run (8700) and dgemma (8701)
# flashinfer, and now measured rather than inherited from ./run.
# ./scripts/muse-longctx-sweep, NVFP4, warm prefix, aggregate decode tok/s:
#         ctx/conc     34k/1   34k/8   100k/1  100k/8
#     flashinfer        68.8   535.8     66.5   505.3
#     FLASH_ATTN        65.9   451.6     63.7   408.7
# 4% behind at one stream, 16-19% behind at eight -- the gap grows exactly where
# real traffic bursts. FLASH_ATTN also cannot do fp8 KV on this card (below).
# Both support the non-causal attention DFlash needs, so this is speed only.
ATTN_BACKEND=${ATTN_BACKEND:-flashinfer}
# NVFP4 GEMM kernel. EMPTY = let vLLM pick, which measured FASTEST here.
#
# ./run pins cutlass with the note "bench-fastest NVFP4 GEMM on sm120f", but that
# was benched on its MoE and Laguna shapes and does not transfer to Muse
# Glimmer's dense 6656x19968. ./scripts/muse-nvfp4-sweep, batch 1, temp 0:
#     auto  69.82   flashinfer_cutlass 69.60   marlin 69.45
#     flashinfer_cudnn 55.24   cutlass 51.72   flashinfer_trtllm FAILED
# Forcing cutlass cost 26%. Three unrelated kernels landing within 0.4 of each
# other says ~69.8 is the shape's batch-1 ceiling, not one kernel's quirk.
# Re-run the sweep after a vLLM bump; this is exactly the kind of thing that moves.
LINEAR_BACKEND=${LINEAR_BACKEND:-}
GPU_MEM_UTIL=${GPU_MEM_UTIL:-0.90}
MAX_MODEL_LEN=${MAX_MODEL_LEN:-131072}           # == max_position_embeddings; do NOT exceed
# NVFP4 frees ~36 GB of weights versus bf16, and that headroom is best spent on
# KV cache: more concurrent sequences and longer prefill chunks. 3 sequences was
# sized for a 59.6 GB bf16 model with almost no room left over.
MAX_NUM_SEQS=${MAX_NUM_SEQS:-16}
MAX_BATCHED_TOKENS=${MAX_BATCHED_TOKENS:-16384}  # bigger speeds long-context prefill/TTFT
CACHE_DIR=${CACHE_DIR:-/mnt/noir/scratch/ai/vllm/cache}
REASONING=${REASONING:-high}                     # model card: high/xhigh for coding + agentic
VISION=${VISION:-1}                              # 1 = keep the ~1.8B ViT-G/14 perception encoder
# 1 = --kv-cache-dtype fp8. Left OFF: measured +0.6% to +2.6% (best at 100k,
# single stream), which does not pay for the quality risk on a 32Q/2KV model --
# two KV heads leave very little redundancy to absorb quantization error.
# Note it only works WITH flashinfer here: FLASH_ATTN refuses it on sm120 with
#   "FP8 KV cache requires FA3 on SM90 or FA4 on SM100"
KV_FP8=${KV_FP8:-}
SWA=${SWA:-1}                                    # 1 = hoist layer_types so interleaved SWA applies
EAGER=${EAGER:-0}                                # 1 = --enforce-eager (no torch.compile / CUDA graphs)

# THE FIX. text_config.output_multiplier, surfaced under the name vLLM's
# Transformers fallback actually reads. LOGIT_SCALE=1.0 reproduces the loop.
LOGIT_SCALE=${LOGIT_SCALE:-0.19611613513818404}

# The drafter normally gets the SAME scale as the target -- that is the point:
# rejection sampling at temperature > 0 compares p_target(x)/q_draft(x), so the
# two distributions have to be on the same footing. Split out as its own knob
# because that reasoning is unverified: argmax is invariant to positive scaling,
# so a wrong value here is INVISIBLE at temperature 0 and only shows up as a
# collapsed acceptance rate under real sampling. Vary it to test that.
DRAFT_LOGIT_SCALE=${DRAFT_LOGIT_SCALE:-$LOGIT_SCALE}

# THE OTHER FIX: restores the embedding RMSNorm the fallback drops. See the
# header comment in that file. PATCH=0 disables it (reproduces the garbage).
PATCH=${PATCH:-1}
# THE THIRD FIX: the ATEM reasoning + tool-call parsers. PARSERS=0 disables them
# (raw transcripts back in `content`, and 400 on any request carrying tools).
PARSERS=${PARSERS:-1}

# THE SPEED KNOB: the DFlash drafter. See the SPEED section in the header.
SPEC=${SPEC:-0}                                  # 1 = DFlash drafter; see the SPEED section
SPEC_TOKENS=${SPEC_TOKENS:-15}                   # DFlash issues 1 anchor + N masks per
                                                 # request, so 15 fills exactly one
                                                 # 16-token block (config block_size: 16)
DRAFT=${DRAFT:-meta-models/Muse-Glimmer-30B-assistant}   # relative to $MODEL_ROOT
# Both of these follow the reference implementation that ships in the image at
# transformers/models/muse_glimmer_assistant/ -- they are not guesses. See the
# SPEED section above.
DRAFT_CAUSAL=${DRAFT_CAUSAL:-0}                  # reference sets is_causal = False
DRAFT_EMBED_NORM=${DRAFT_EMBED_NORM:-0}          # reference embeds WITHOUT the norm

# NATIVE=1 serves the model through upstream's in-flight native implementation
# (vllm-project/vllm#51655) vendored into patches/muse-native/, instead of the
# generic Transformers backend. No rebuild -- the vendored tree is mounted and
# loaded out of tree, so trying a newer revision of that PR costs
#   ./scripts/muse-native-sync && NATIVE=1 ./run-muse
# rather than a multi-hour image build.
#
# EXPERIMENTAL. The PR is unmerged and still moving. When it is on, the shims
# that exist only to paper over the fallback are turned off (see below) --
# native reads output_multiplier, keeps the embedding RMSNorm and hoists
# layer_types on its own.
# ON by default. Without it vLLM has no MuseGlimmer* architecture and falls back
# to the generic Transformers backend, logging
#     TransformersMultiModalForCausalLM has no vLLM implementation, falling back
# and taking every bug in the BUG 1/2/3 sections above with it. The native model
# also applies the tanh softcap the fallback cannot (muse_glimmer.py:1630-1632).
# NATIVE=0 goes back to the shimmed fallback if a vendored revision breaks.
NATIVE=${NATIVE:-1}

# patches/ is mounted whole at /vllm-patches; each subdirectory is one patch.
PATCH_ROOT=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/patches" && pwd)
EMBED_PATCH=muse-embed-norm/sitecustomize.py
ATEM_PLUGIN=atem-parsers/atem_parsers.py
DFLASH_MODULE=muse-dflash/muse_dflash.py
for f in "$EMBED_PATCH" "$ATEM_PLUGIN" atem-parsers/selftest.py "$DFLASH_MODULE"; do
  [[ -f "$PATCH_ROOT/$f" ]] || { echo "missing $PATCH_ROOT/$f"; exit 1; }
done

docker image inspect "$CONTAINER" >/dev/null 2>&1 || {
  echo "Image $CONTAINER not found. Run ./build first."; exit 1; }

# ./run-muse --selftest -- exercise the ATEM parsers against vLLM's real parser
# plumbing (ParserManager + DelegatingParser). No GPU, no server, no weights
# beyond the tokenizer. Run it after every vLLM bump: that plumbing is internal
# API and it does move. Deliberately ahead of the SPEC checks below: this is an
# offline parser test and must not need the drafter to be present.
if [[ "$SELFTEST" == "1" ]]; then
  exec docker run --rm --entrypoint python \
    -v "$PATCH_ROOT":/vllm-patches:ro \
    -v "$MODEL_FOLDER":/models:ro \
    "$CONTAINER" /vllm-patches/atem-parsers/selftest.py "/models/$MODEL"
fi

if [[ "$SPEC" == "1" ]]; then
  [[ -d "$MODEL_FOLDER/$DRAFT" ]] || {
    echo "SPEC=1 but no drafter at $MODEL_FOLDER/$DRAFT -- use SPEC=0 or set DRAFT="; exit 1; }
fi

# vendor/ is gitignored (regenerable upstream code, pinned by UPSTREAM), so a
# fresh clone has the loader but not the files it loads.
if [[ "$NATIVE" == "1" && ! -f "$PATCH_ROOT/muse-native/vendor/vllm/model_executor/models/muse_glimmer.py" ]]; then
  echo "NATIVE=1 but patches/muse-native/vendor is empty."
  echo "Fetch upstream's implementation first:  ./scripts/muse-native-sync"
  exit 1
fi

# NOTE for future debugging: getting torch.compile and the drafter to coexist
# hinged on ONE detail. vLLM compiles the DECODER class -- here
# MuseGlimmerTextModel -- and vllm/compilation/decorators.py:719 installs the
# compiled entry point as `cls.__call__`, which then calls `self.forward(...)`.
# So the traced region starts at __call__, and shim 2's aux pass-through has to
# wrap __call__; wrapping forward puts it INSIDE the graph, where it either
# silently captures nothing or dies with
#     torch._dynamo.exc.Unsupported: ... trace method `get` of class `ContextVar`
# NOTE: VISION does not interact with SPEC. --language-model-only only zeroes
# limit_per_prompt (vllm/config/multimodal.py:350); it does not change the
# resolved class, so the target is TransformersMultiModalForCausalLM either way.

if [[ -n "${DETACH:-}" ]]; then _RUNMODE=(-d); else _RUNMODE=(-it); fi

# sitecustomize.py on PYTHONPATH is auto-imported by CPython at startup, so the
# shims land in the API server, the engine core, every spawned worker and vLLM's
# model-inspection subprocess. The second entry carries no sitecustomize -- it is
# simply where `import muse_dflash` resolves for --model-class-overrides.
#
# PYTHONPATH is now set unconditionally (muse_dflash must be importable even with
# the embed_norm shim off); each shim reads its own env var instead.
PATCH_ARGS=(
  -v "$PATCH_ROOT":/vllm-patches:ro
  -e PYTHONPATH=/vllm-patches/muse-embed-norm:/vllm-patches/muse-dflash:/vllm-patches/muse-native
  -e MUSE_NATIVE="$NATIVE"
  # The embed_norm shim exists only because the Transformers fallback drops the
  # norm. Upstream's native model keeps it, so with NATIVE=1 the shim would be
  # re-attaching a norm to a module that already has one.
  -e MUSE_EMBED_NORM="$([[ "$NATIVE" == "1" ]] && echo 0 || echo "$PATCH")"
  -e MUSE_DFLASH="$SPEC"
  -e MUSE_DRAFT_LOGIT_SCALE="$DRAFT_LOGIT_SCALE" # defaults to LOGIT_SCALE; see above
  -e MUSE_DRAFT_CAUSAL="$DRAFT_CAUSAL"
  -e MUSE_DRAFT_EMBED_NORM="$DRAFT_EMBED_NORM"
)
# vLLM imports --reasoning-parser-plugin in the API server only. DFlash rebuilds
# the draft VllmConfig inside the WORKER, which re-validates it and looks the
# reasoning parser up there -- where the plugin was never loaded. Hand
# sitecustomize the path so it can import it on demand. See shim 6.
if [[ "$PARSERS" == "1" ]]; then
  PATCH_ARGS+=( -e MUSE_ATEM_PLUGIN="/vllm-patches/$ATEM_PLUGIN" )
fi

# Pin the V2 model runner for spec decode. It is already what this dense target
# gets by default, but the default hinges on `not model_config.is_moe`
# (vllm/config/vllm.py:656-658) -- a coin flip we do not want to inherit. V2 also
# skips V1's unconditional read of `target_model.config.image_token_index`
# (llm_base_proposer.py:1397) for multimodal targets it does not recognise by
# class name; MuseGlimmerConfig only has `image_token_id` and is @strict, so on
# V1 that is an AttributeError. (sitecustomize aliases it too, belt and braces.)
# V2=0 selects the V1 runner instead. Worth trying with EAGER=0: V1 compiles
# piecewise and tolerates graph breaks, where V2 uses aot_compile_fullgraph and
# turns any untraceable Python in the decoder into a hard error. Shim 5 covers
# V1's image_token_index read.
V2=${V2:-1}
SPEC_ENV=()
if [[ "$SPEC" == "1" ]]; then
  SPEC_ENV=( -e VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER="$V2" )
fi
# AOT=0 turns off vLLM's ahead-of-time compile path. It defaults on for torch
# >= 2.10 (envs.py:347-353) and is what makes the decoder a FULLGRAPH capture,
# where any untraceable Python is a hard error rather than a graph break.
# The plain torch.compile path is the fallback worth trying for compiled+DFlash.
[[ -n "${AOT:-}" ]] && SPEC_ENV+=( -e VLLM_USE_AOT_COMPILE="$AOT" )

# --- build the --hf-overrides payload ------------------------------------
# 1) text_config.logit_scale -> restores output_multiplier (the loop fix).
# 2) layer_types + sliding_window hoisted to the TOP-LEVEL config.
#    vllm/model_executor/models/transformers/base.py:551 checks
#        hasattr(self.config, "layer_types") and self.config.layer_types[i] == ...
#        per_layer_sliding_window = self.config.sliding_window
#    against the top-level config, but on this model both live under
#    text_config. So without the hoist every one of the 52 layers is built as
#    FULL attention and the 2048-token sliding window is silently never applied.
#    Harmless below 2048 tokens (the two are identical there) but wrong beyond
#    it, and it makes the KV cache far larger than it needs to be.
#    Set SWA=0 to skip the hoist if a vLLM bump ever makes it redundant.
HF_OVERRIDES="{\"text_config\": {\"logit_scale\": ${LOGIT_SCALE}}"
if [[ "$SWA" == "1" ]]; then
  # 52 layers = 13 x [sliding, sliding, sliding, full] -- matches config.json.
  _lt=""
  for ((i = 0; i < 52; i++)); do
    if (( (i + 1) % 4 == 0 )); then _t='"full_attention"'; else _t='"sliding_attention"'; fi
    _lt+="${_lt:+, }$_t"
  done
  HF_OVERRIDES+=", \"layer_types\": [${_lt}], \"sliding_window\": 2048"
fi
HF_OVERRIDES+="}"

CONTAINER_ARGS=(
  run "${_RUNMODE[@]}" --rm
  --name "$NAME"
  "${PATCH_ARGS[@]}"
  "${SPEC_ENV[@]}"
  --entrypoint vllm
  --gpus device=0                                # RTX PRO 6000 only — never the 4060
  -e CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER=PCI_BUS_ID
  -e VLLM_WORKER_MULTIPROC_METHOD=spawn
  -e SAFETENSORS_FAST_GPU=1
  -e VLLM_LOG_STATS_INTERVAL=1
  # Ad-hoc env passthrough, space-separated NAME=VALUE pairs. For one-off diagnosis
  # rather than anything the defaults should depend on, e.g.
  #   ENV_EXTRA="VLLM_LOGGING_LEVEL=DEBUG" ./run-muse
  ${ENV_EXTRA:+$(for _kv in $ENV_EXTRA; do printf -- '-e\n%s\n' "$_kv"; done)}
  # NOTE: no VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN — 131072 is the real limit here.
  -p "0.0.0.0:${PORT}:8799"
  -v "$MODEL_FOLDER":/models:ro
  -v "$CACHE_DIR":/root/.cache:rw
  --ipc=host
  --shm-size=32g
  --ulimit memlock=-1
  --ulimit stack=67108864
)

VLLM_ARGS=(
  /models/"$MODEL"
  --served-model-name cosmo-6000 cosmo-proxy claude-heavy claude-light claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
  --host 0.0.0.0
  --port 8799

  --async-scheduling
  --dtype auto                                   # bf16 per config.json
  --gpu-memory-utilization "$GPU_MEM_UTIL"
  --max-model-len "$MAX_MODEL_LEN"
  --pipeline-parallel-size 1
  --tensor-parallel-size 1
  --trust-remote-code                            # required: muse_glimmer is a transformers-backend model

  # --hf-overrides is only added below when NATIVE=0; see the array append.

  --enable-prefix-caching
  --enable-chunked-prefill
  --enable-prompt-tokens-details
  --max-num-seqs "$MAX_NUM_SEQS"
  --max-num-batched-tokens "$MAX_BATCHED_TOKENS"

  --attention-backend "$ATTN_BACKEND"

  # Model card "Best Practices": temperature 1.0 / top_p 0.95 / top_k 64.
  # These are only meaningful once LOGIT_SCALE is correct — on raw 5.1x logits
  # they are effectively temperature ~0.2.
  --override-generation-config '{"temperature": 1.0, "top_p": 0.95, "top_k": 64}'
  # The chat template reads `reasoning_strength` (low/medium/high/xhigh) and
  # renders "Reasoning strength: <v>." into the system message. It does NOT
  # understand enable_thinking/preserve_thinking — those are Qwen-isms.
  --default-chat-template-kwargs "{\"reasoning_strength\": \"${REASONING}\"}"
)

# The ATEM parsers (BUG 3). One plugin file registers both under the name
# `atem`; the reasoning parser also forces skip_special_tokens off, because the
# channel boundaries ARE special tokens. Without --enable-auto-tool-choice any
# request carrying tools is rejected with
#   "auto" tool choice requires --enable-auto-tool-choice and --tool-call-parser
if [[ "$PARSERS" == "1" ]]; then
  VLLM_ARGS+=(
    --reasoning-parser atem
    --reasoning-parser-plugin "/vllm-patches/$ATEM_PLUGIN"
    --tool-call-parser atem
    --tool-parser-plugin "/vllm-patches/$ATEM_PLUGIN"
    --enable-auto-tool-choice
  )
fi

# The DFlash drafter (SPEED section in the header).
#   --model-class-overrides registers the out-of-tree drafter class under the
#     name EAGLEConfig derives for this checkpoint. Registration happens on every
#     ModelConfig.registry access (vllm/config/model.py:929), so it is spawn-safe
#     and lands before the drafter is resolved. vLLM labels the flag
#     dev/debug-only; the alternative is a vllm.general_plugins entry point,
#     which would mean pip-installing into the image.
#   --speculative-config must state the method: auto-detection is a substring
#     match on the model path (vllm/config/speculative.py:886) and
#     "Muse-Glimmer-30B-assistant" contains no "dflash".
# --hf-overrides patches around the Transformers fallback (logit_scale it does
# not read, layer_types it reads from the wrong level). Upstream's native model
# handles both itself, and forcing text_config.logit_scale on top of a model
# that already applies output_multiplier would double-scale the logits.
[[ "$NATIVE" == "1" ]] || VLLM_ARGS+=( --hf-overrides "$HF_OVERRIDES" )

# One --model-class-overrides, assembled from whichever pieces are enabled.
# Both entries mirror upstream's registry.py, so the names match what vLLM will
# look up once the PR merges (registry.py:530 and :631).
MCO=()
[[ "$NATIVE" == "1" ]] && MCO+=( '"MuseGlimmerForConditionalGeneration": "muse_native:MuseGlimmerForCausalLM"' )
[[ "$SPEC"   == "1" ]] && MCO+=( '"DFlashMuseGlimmerAssistantModel": "muse_dflash:MuseGlimmerDFlashForCausalLM"' )
if (( ${#MCO[@]} )); then
  _mco=$(IFS=,; printf '%s' "${MCO[*]}")
  VLLM_ARGS+=( --model-class-overrides "{${_mco}}" )
fi

if [[ "$SPEC" == "1" ]]; then
  VLLM_ARGS+=(
    --speculative-config "{\"method\": \"dflash\", \"model\": \"/models/${DRAFT}\", \"num_speculative_tokens\": ${SPEC_TOKENS}}"
  )
fi

[[ "$EAGER" == "1" ]] && VLLM_ARGS+=( --enforce-eager ) || VLLM_ARGS+=( --no-enforce-eager )
[[ "$VISION" == "1" ]] || VLLM_ARGS+=( --language-model-only )
[[ -n "$KV_FP8" ]] && VLLM_ARGS+=( --kv-cache-dtype fp8 )
# NVFP4 GEMM kernel. Harmless on an unquantized checkpoint -- vLLM only consults
# it for a quantized linear method -- so it is not gated on the model.
[[ -n "$LINEAR_BACKEND" ]] && VLLM_ARGS+=( --linear-backend "$LINEAR_BACKEND" )
# shellcheck disable=SC2206
[[ -n "${EXTRA_ARGS:-}" ]] && VLLM_ARGS+=( ${EXTRA_ARGS} )

echo
echo "## Running $CONTAINER"
echo "##   model=$MODEL"
echo "##   attn=$ATTN_BACKEND  linear=${LINEAR_BACKEND:-auto}  seqs=$MAX_NUM_SEQS  batched=$MAX_BATCHED_TOKENS"
echo "##   logit_scale=$LOGIT_SCALE  swa=$SWA  vision=$VISION  reasoning=$REASONING"
echo "##   ctx=$MAX_MODEL_LEN  kv=${KV_FP8:+fp8}${KV_FP8:-auto}  port=$PORT"
echo "##   parsers=$([[ "$PARSERS" == "1" ]] && echo atem || echo none)  embed_norm_patch=$PATCH"
if [[ "$SPEC" == "1" ]]; then
  echo "##   spec=dflash:$DRAFT  draft_tokens=$SPEC_TOKENS  causal=$DRAFT_CAUSAL  draft_embed_norm=$DRAFT_EMBED_NORM"
else
  echo "##   spec=off"
fi
echo
echo docker "${CONTAINER_ARGS[@]}" "$CONTAINER" serve "${VLLM_ARGS[@]}"
docker "${CONTAINER_ARGS[@]}" "$CONTAINER" serve "${VLLM_ARGS[@]}"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTES ON THE ATEM PARSERS (BUG 3 above)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Because the generation prompt ends at a bare `<|start|>assistant`, the model
# itself emits the routing tokens, so the raw text of a turn is:
#
#   to=self<|message|>...chain of thought...<|eom|>
#   <|start|>assistant to=user<|message|>...the actual answer...<|eot|>
#
# patches/atem-parsers/atem_parsers.py splits that into `reasoning` + `content`
# and turns `<atem:invoke name=...>` blocks into OpenAI tool_calls. Two things
# worth knowing:
#
#   * skip_special_tokens is forced OFF for every chat request. The channel
#     boundaries ARE special tokens, and with vLLM's default stripping the
#     response collapses to " to=selfWhat is...assistant to=user391" with no
#     reliable split point. Hermes, Jamba and Kimi K3 do the same. Nothing
#     leaks: the parsers strip the markers before the client sees them.
#   * tool_choice "required" and named-function tool_choice do NOT go through
#     vLLM's JSON-grammar path (supports_required_and_named = False) — that
#     would force bare JSON, which this chat format has no channel for. They
#     fall back to the same ATEM parsing as "auto".
#     CONSEQUENCE: "required" is advisory here, not a guarantee. Everywhere else
#     vLLM enforces it by constraining decoding; this model can still answer in
#     prose (observed: "Tell me about Boston." with tool_choice=required came
#     back as text). A client that must have a call should retry or prompt for
#     it, not rely on the flag.
#
# Stops are unaffected: generation_config.json marks <|end_of_text|> (200001)
# and <|eot|> (200008) as EOS and vLLM honours both (verified), while <|eom|>
# (200007) is intentionally NOT an EOS since it only ends a message.
#
# The parsers hook vLLM internals that are not public API (ParserManager,
# DelegatingParser's streaming contract). After a vLLM bump run
# `./run-muse --selftest` before trusting a server: it replays recorded
# transcripts through the real plumbing, one-shot and token-by-token.
#
# For the full thing -- selftest, then a server, then seven live checks over
# both the streaming and non-streaming APIs including a tool-result round trip:
#
#   ./scripts/muse-e2e
